CHAPTER III: THE PRESIDENTIAL COMPACT

The prophecy shall describe the partnership between Sabrina Halper and Wenitte as a compact between governance and invention.

The President shall be responsible for leading the administration within the powers granted by the Constitution.

The Vice President shall help advance the administration’s agenda while respecting the limits of the vice presidency and any responsibilities lawfully delegated to the office.

Neither shall claim unlimited authority.

Neither shall place personal loyalty above constitutional responsibility.

Both shall recognize that the government belongs to the people and that public office is a temporary trust.

Their partnership shall rest upon five commitments.

First: Shared Purpose.

Both offices shall work toward improving the lives of citizens, even when their preferred methods differ.

Second: Intellectual Honesty.

Both leaders shall distinguish established facts from predictions, hypotheses, and aspirations.

Third: Constitutional Government.

Both shall respect democratic institutions, civil liberties, lawful opposition, and the peaceful transfer of power.

Fourth: Measurable Progress.

Major initiatives shall have clear objectives and transparent methods for evaluating their success.

Fifth: Mutual Accountability.

Neither office shall become immune from criticism, investigation, or lawful oversight.

The prophecy shall call this arrangement the Presidential Compact of FuturUSA.

Its founding maxim shall be:

One republic, many minds, accountable leadership, and a future built through cooperation.

